{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% from "_macros.html.j2" import money, estimate %}
{% from "_site.html.j2" import waitlist, pending, scroll_table %}
{% block title %}Loom: measured cost per token for open-weight models{% endblock %}
{% block content %}
<header class="page-head">
<h1>Open-weight model inference, priced from measurements</h1>
<p class="lede">Loom is an inference service for open-weight models, in development. We publish measured quality, latency, throughput and cost per token — and how prices are derived from them. Every number links to the exact configuration and provenance that produced it, and the harness that measured it is open source.</p>
</header>

{% if manifest.empty %}
{{ pending("The benchmark harness is built and tested against a simulated GPU; no GPU runs have been published. The table below lists the models and configurations queued for the first runs, and fills in from the results snapshot once they complete.") }}
{% endif %}

<section aria-labelledby="models-h">
<h2 id="models-h">Models</h2>
{% if manifest.empty %}
<p class="section-note">Configurations come from the model registry, <a href="{{ registry_url }}">config/models.yaml</a>.</p>
{% call scroll_table("models-h") %}
<table>
<thead>
<tr><th scope="col">Model</th><th scope="col">Engine</th><th scope="col">Hardware</th><th scope="col">Precision</th><th scope="col">$/1M output tokens at SLO</th><th scope="col">Status</th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
{% for m in models %}
<tr>
<td class="model"><a href="{{ root }}{{ m.path }}"><strong>{{ m.snap.display_name }}</strong></a><span class="sub">{{ m.snap.repo or '' }}</span></td>
{% if m.planned %}
<td class="nowrap">{{ m.planned.engine }}</td>
<td>{{ m.planned.hardware }}</td>
<td>{{ m.planned.quantization }}</td>
{% else %}
<td colspan="3">not in the registry</td>
{% endif %}
<td class="muted">not measured yet</td>
<td><span class="badge pending">first runs pending</span></td>
</tr>
{% endfor %}
</tbody>
</table>
{% endcall %}
{% else %}
<p class="section-note">Per benchmarked workload, the best configuration: the cheapest at SLO among configs that passed every check. A candidate (another precision, engine or setting) is ranked only once its quality gate passes against the model's BF16 reference; a failed or inconclusive gate keeps it out, however cheap. Where no config is ranked the row says why, and an untrusted reference is shown with its flag as a comparison point, never as the best config. $/1M input and $/1M output split the replica's on-demand cost by measured prefill time (<a href="{{ root }}methodology.html#split">how</a>). Values are point estimates (geometric means for latency and throughput); the line under each is its {{ (manifest.confidence * 100)|round|int }}% confidence interval. SLO: {{ describe_slo(manifest.slo) if manifest.slo else 'not recorded' }}.</p>
{% call scroll_table("models-h") %}
<table class="headline">
<thead>
<tr><th scope="col">Workload</th><th scope="col">Best config at SLO</th><th scope="col" class="num">$/1M input,<br>on-demand</th><th scope="col" class="num">$/1M output,<br>on-demand</th><th scope="col" class="num">Goodput out tok/s per GPU</th><th scope="col" class="num">p95 TTFT</th><th scope="col" class="num">p95 TPOT</th><th scope="col">Quality gate</th></tr>
</thead>
{% for m in models %}
<tbody>
<tr class="group"><th scope="rowgroup" colspan="8"><a href="{{ root }}{{ m.path }}">{{ m.snap.display_name }}</a> <span class="repo">{{ m.snap.repo or '' }}</span></th></tr>
{% for h in headline if h.model is sameas m %}
<tr class="{{ 'ranked' if h.best else 'unranked' }}">
{% if h.board is none %}
<td colspan="8" class="muted">No published results for this model yet — first runs pending.</td>
{% elif h.quoted is none %}
<td class="workload"><a href="{{ root }}{{ m.path }}#{{ h.board.anchor }}">{{ h.board.title }}</a></td>
<td colspan="7" class="muted wrap">No config ranked: {{ h.board.basis }}. Details on the model page.</td>
{% else %}
{% set q = h.quoted %}
{% set r = q.result %}
{% set split_in, split_out, _ = split_ranges(r) %}
<td class="workload"><a href="{{ root }}{{ m.path }}#{{ h.board.anchor }}">{{ h.board.title }}</a></td>
<td class="cfg">{% if h.best %}<strong>{{ r.name }}</strong>{% else %}<span class="muted">No config ranked.</span> Comparison point: <strong>{{ r.name }}</strong> <span class="badge {{ q.status.name|lower }}">{{ q.status.value }}, not ranked</span>{% endif %}<span class="sub">{{ r.label.short }}</span>{% if not h.best %}<span class="sub">{{ unranked_reason(r)|sentence }}</span>{% endif %}</td>
<td class="num">{{ money(split_in) }}</td>
<td class="num">{{ money(split_out) }}</td>
<td class="num">{{ estimate(r.goodput_output_tok_s_per_gpu, 1) }}</td>
<td class="num">{{ estimate(r.ttft_p95_ms, 0, 'ms') }}</td>
<td class="num">{{ estimate(r.tpot_p95_ms, 1, 'ms') }}</td>
<td>{% if r.quality and r.quality.gate %}<span class="badge {{ r.quality.gate }}">{{ gate_label(r.quality.gate) }}</span>{% if r.quality.gate != 'baseline' %}<span class="sub">vs {{ r.quality.baseline_text }}</span>{% else %}<span class="sub">the BF16 reference</span>{% endif %}{% elif r.quality and r.quality.tasks %}<span class="muted">scored, no gate</span>{% else %}<span class="muted">not evaluated</span>{% endif %}</td>
{% endif %}
</tr>
{% endfor %}
</tbody>
{% endfor %}
</table>
{% endcall %}
<p class="section-note">{{ manifest.experiment_ids|length }} experiment{{ '' if manifest.experiment_ids|length == 1 else 's' }}, {{ manifest.run_count }} runs. Cost is at the on-demand list price of the replica's instance plus its storage volume; see <a href="{{ root }}methodology.html#cost">how cost is derived</a> and <a href="{{ root }}pricing.html">how it compares with public list prices</a>.</p>
{% endif %}
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="read-h">
<h2 id="read-h">What the numbers mean</h2>
<dl class="defs">
<dt>Goodput at SLO</dt>
<dd>The highest tested load at which latency and errors stay within the service-level objective, judged on the upper end of the confidence interval. Raw peak throughput is reported separately and never used for cost. <a href="{{ root }}methodology.html#goodput">Definition</a></dd>
<dt>Cost per token</dt>
<dd>The replica's hourly on-demand list price (instance plus storage volume) divided by the tokens it produces per hour at goodput, split between input and output tokens by the measured share of time spent prefilling prompts. Spot and as-run costs are shown on each model page. Prices come from public price pages, each with its source and check date. <a href="{{ root }}methodology.html#cost">Formula and worked example</a></dd>
<dt>Quality</dt>
<dd>Each configuration is scored on pinned evaluation sets against the BF16 reference configuration of the same model. Only a gate pass ranks a candidate; one whose gate failed or is inconclusive is listed with the reason but never ranked. <a href="{{ root }}methodology.html#quality">Gate rule</a></dd>
</dl>
</section>

{{ waitlist(config) }}
{% endblock %}
